Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["To CodeX", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9650328150787077`*^9, 3.965032820124859*^9}, {
  3.968695027315658*^9, 3.9686950835806055`*^9}, {3.9696636787370167`*^9, 
  3.9696636827400074`*^9}, {3.9701051839257464`*^9, 3.9701051849638495`*^9}, {
  3.994818307660136*^9, 
  3.994818311292067*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c5f5f998-5607-45d9-949d-\
0c33b5810901"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "[Run1:  Data Point]\nMake .json file that will be used in the fit analysis \
as data inputs. Files are saved in Stan_inputs/\n\n[Run2:  Form Factor] and \
[Run3:  Observables]\nMake Stan_FitFunction.wls module to produce the fit \
functions. Selection of FF parameterization should be specified an argument. \
Integration part should be skipped if there already exists the output in \
Stan_inputs/\n\n[Run4:  Common Setup] and [Stan Code Generator:  fit \
procedure (B-PDG)]\nAs for prior of the FF parameters, follow \
My_2606.17138v1.tex. Option for the prior is not needed. \n\nAs for Unitary \
Bound (UB) fit part, the code can specify the fit model from 3 cases: \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]no-UB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]soft-UB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], and \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]hard-UB\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] according to \
UBmodel.md.\n\nAs for the generator of .stan file, CodeX already wrote \
StanCodeGenerator_BPDG_Modular.wl by following my suggestions. But check and \
modify it to satisfy the above code development. Rename the code file at \
Stan_CodeGenerator.wls\n\n[Overall]\nMake a single main code that (1) \
generates an executable stan file (using the above modules) and (2) then \
perform the MCMC fit. Name should be Stan_FitAnalysis.py. \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["CutControl",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] option should be given in the main code, not by \
argument. My original code is \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]ParameterFit_ControlCenter_v1.2_ScenarioB.py\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. But this corresponds to just (2). \n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.963626433490946*^9, 3.96362656116815*^9}, {
   3.968560053535117*^9, 3.9685600803046937`*^9}, {3.968560110973036*^9, 
